B.f60=new A.y("Hormones","Two small glands on top of the kidneys. They make adrenaline, the hormone that gets you ready to run or fight.")
B.eLM=new A.y("Hormones",'A pea-sized gland under the brain. It is the "master gland" that tells your other glands what to do.')
B.eLH=new A.y("Defence","A small gland behind the breastbone where young white blood cells learn to fight germs. It is biggest in children.")
B.eYi=new A.y("Senses","A strong muscle covered in about 10,000 taste buds. It helps you taste, chew, swallow and talk.")
B.eZf=new A.y("Breathing","The larynx holds your vocal cords. Air makes them buzz, and your mouth shapes the buzz into words. The epiglottis is a flap that stops food going down your windpipe.")
B.eYe=new A.y("Frame","Soft, spongy cushions between your vertebrae. They absorb shocks when you walk and jump. You are slightly taller in the morning because the discs fill up with water at night.")
B.eJK=new A.y("Digestion","Adults have 32 teeth. The outside, called enamel, is the hardest substance in your body.")
B.eW9=new A.y("Movement","Many layers of muscles along your spine keep you standing tall and let you bend and twist.")
B.f68=new A.y("Breathing","Muscles between your ribs lift the rib cage to help you breathe in and out.")
B.eZB=new A.y("Movement","You have over 40 muscles in your face. A smile uses about 12 of them. Others move your eyes and jaw.")
B.ePc=new A.y("Movement","Small muscles in your feet curl your toes and hold up the arch of your foot.")
B.eJo=new A.y("Movement","These lift your leg forward when you walk and keep your hips steady.")
B.eOd=new A.y("Movement","They pull your legs together and help you balance.")
B.eQa=new A.y("Movement","A sling of muscles at the bottom of your pelvis that holds up the organs above it.")
B.eLV=new A.y("Movement","Four small muscles that hold your arm bone in your shoulder socket and let you rotate your arm.")
B.f3q=new A.y("Blood","Strong tubes carrying fresh, oxygen-rich blood away from the heart to every part of you.")
B.f4C=new A.y("Blood","Tubes that bring used blood back to the heart. Tiny valves inside stop the blood flowing backwards.")
B.eVU=new A.y("Blood","The coronary arteries and veins feed the heart muscle itself. The heart needs its own supply of blood to keep beating.")
B.f4l=new A.y("Cover","Your biggest organ. It keeps water in and germs out, and sheds about 30,000 dead cells every minute.")
B.eUs=new A.y("Skin","Your head holds your brain, eyes, ears, nose and mouth. It weighs about 5 kg, as much as a bag of sugar.")
B.eZJ=new A.y("Skin","You have about 100,000 hairs on your head. Each grows about a centimetre a month.")
B.eJv=new A.y("Senses","Your eyes turn light into signals for the brain. Each one sends the picture upside down and the brain flips it.")
B.eQy=new A.y("Senses","Ears hear sounds and also keep you balanced. The three tiny bones inside are the smallest in your body.")
B.eZo=new A.y("Senses","You can smell about a trillion different smells. Your nose also warms and cleans the air you breathe.")
B.eUO=new A.y("Senses","Your lips have lots of touch nerves and thin skin, which is why they are red.")
B.f4t=new A.y("Frame","Your neck holds your head up and carries the windpipe, food pipe, blood vessels and nerves.")
B.eXJ=new A.y("Cover","Your trunk holds your heart, lungs and digestive system, protected by skin, muscle and bone.")
B.eJI=new A.y("Movement","Each arm has 30 bones. Your elbow bends one way and your shoulder moves in almost any direction.")
B.f_k=new A.y("Touch","Each hand has 27 bones and thousands of touch sensors. Fingertips are some of the most sensitive spots.")
B.f33=new A.y("Movement","Your legs have the biggest muscles and the longest bones in your body.")
B.f19=new A.y("Balance","Each foot has 26 bones and about 125,000 sweat glands. Together they carry your whole weight.")
B.eHI=new A.y("Movement","These muscles turn and tilt your head. Your head weighs as much as a bowling ball, so they work all day.")
B.eXr=new A.y("Movement","A big kite-shaped muscle across your upper back that lifts your shoulders and moves your head.")
B.eXv=new A.y("Movement","The round caps of your shoulders. They lift your arms in every direction.")
B.eRi=new A.y("Movement","The chest muscles push your arms forward, like when you push a door.")
B.eMc=new A.y("Movement","The biceps bends your elbow. When a muscle works it gets shorter and fatter.")
B.ePZ=new A.y("Movement","The triceps straightens your elbow. It works opposite the biceps: muscles can only pull, so they come in pairs.")
B.eWk=new A.y("Movement","Long muscles in your forearm pull on tendons that work your fingers, like puppet strings.")
B.f2_=new A.y("Movement","Your tummy muscles hold your body upright and help you bend and twist.")
B.f65=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the sides of your waist that help you twist and lean.")
B.eZG=new A.y("Movement","The widest muscle in your back. It pulls your arms down, like when you swim or climb.")
B.eHn=new A.y("Movement","Your bottom muscles are the biggest in your body. They push you up stairs and keep you standing.")
B.eWw=new A.y("Movement","Four muscles at the front of your thigh. Together they are the strongest in your body for lifting weight.")
B.eIh=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the back of your thigh that bend your knee when you run.")
B.f2f=new A.y("Movement","The calf muscle pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.")
B.f3m=new A.y("Movement","These lift your foot up so your toes do not drag on the ground.")
B.eWY=new A.y("Nerves","Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells and runs everything you do.")
B.f2u=new A.y("Hormones","A butterfly-shaped gland in your neck. It makes hormones that control how fast your body uses energy.")
B.eJx=new A.y("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.f4_=new A.y("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.eNA=new A.y("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.f1D=new A.y("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.eQX=new A.y("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.eUI=new A.y("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.f_0=new A.y("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.f49=new A.y("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.f41=new A.y("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.f45=new A.y("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.eVg=new A.y("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
B.f_W=new A.y("Digestion","About 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. This is where most food is turned into energy for your blood.")
B.f16=new A.y("Digestion","Takes the water from what is left and makes the rest into waste. It is about 1.5 metres long.")
B.f3M=new A.y("Cleaning","A stretchy bag that holds urine. It can hold about half a litre.")
B.eWX=new A.y("Nerves","A thick rope of nerves inside your backbone. It carries messages between your brain and the rest of your body.")
B.eT1=new A.y("Frame","Your skull is made of 22 bones that protect your brain. Only the jaw can move.")
B.eRK=new A.y("Frame","The only bone in your skull that moves. You use it to chew, talk and smile.")
B.eXl=new A.y("Frame","Seven small bones called cervical vertebrae. A giraffe has seven too, just much longer!")
B.eZU=new A.y("Frame","Twelve vertebrae that each hold a pair of ribs.")
B.eTy=new A.y("Frame","Five big, strong vertebrae that carry most of your upper body's weight.")
B.eUf=new A.y("Frame","The sacrum and coccyx. The tailbone is what is left of a tail from our far-off ancestors.")
B.eNY=new A.y("Frame","You have 12 pairs of ribs. They make a cage that protects your heart and lungs and moves when you breathe.")
B.f3i=new A.y("Frame","The sternum is a flat bone in the middle of your chest that holds your ribs together at the front.")
B.eON=new A.y("Frame","The most often broken bone, and the only long bone that lies sideways.")
B.eIe=new A.y("Frame","Two flat triangle bones on your back that let your arms swing in a big circle.")
B.eRh=new A.y("Frame",'The humerus. The bump at its end is the "funny bone": really a nerve that gets squashed.')
B.eI9=new A.y("Frame","Two bones, the radius and ulna, that twist round each other when you turn your hand over.")
B.eMF=new A.y("Frame","Eight small wrist bones plus the long bones of your palm and fingers: 27 in all.")
B.eRm=new A.y("Frame","The hip bones carry your body's weight and protect organs in your tummy.")
B.eOW=new A.y("Frame","The femur is the longest and strongest bone in your body, about a quarter of your height.")
B.f_g=new A.y("Frame","A small bone that shields your knee joint, like a built-in knee pad.")
B.eQd=new A.y("Frame","The tibia carries most of your weight below the knee. The thin fibula next to it helps hold the ankle steady.")
B.f5N=new A.y("Frame","Seven ankle bones and long toe bones. Your big toe is important for balance.")
B.eRU=new A.y("Blood","The biggest artery, about as wide as a garden hose. It carries fresh blood from the heart to the whole body.")
